WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.870
Run your finger along the
inside of a garden hose.

2
00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:04.550
It's smooth.

3
00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:07.470
Now picture the lining
of your small intestine.

4
00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:09.070
It isn't smooth at all.

5
00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:11.530
It's covered in millions of tiny,

6
00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:15.710
finger-like bumps called villi,
like the loops on a towel.

7
00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:18.850
Why would your body line
a tube like a towel?

8
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:22.260
In this mission, you'll follow
digested food to the place where

9
00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:23.930
it's absorbed into the blood.

10
00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:27.010
You'll find out what villi do
to the surface of the gut.

11
00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:30.970
And you'll see why thin walls
and a rich blood supply matter

12
00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:32.090
too.

13
00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:35.930
Your mission: explain why your
small intestine is lined like a

14
00:00:35.980 --> 00:00:36.900
towel.
